# CODEOWNERS: who must approve a change
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# The ruleset on main and milestone/** requires a code owner's approval. The last
# matching pattern wins.

# Default: the maintainer owns everything.
*                       @strausmann

# Security-relevant code and configuration, listed explicitly so they stay owned
# even if the default above is ever narrowed.
/app/Authorization/     @strausmann
/app/Identity/          @strausmann
/app/Mfa/               @strausmann
/app/Tokens/            @strausmann
/app/Invitations/       @strausmann
/app/Catalog/           @strausmann
/config/                @strausmann
/docker/                @strausmann
/.github/               @strausmann
/SECURITY.md            @strausmann
/LICENSE                @strausmann
/CLA.md                 @strausmann
/licence-policy.yml     @strausmann
/.releaserc.json        @strausmann
/CONTRIBUTING.md        @strausmann
/README.md              @strausmann
/docs/dockerhub/        @strausmann

# Files that hold nothing but dependency versions have no code owner, so a
# Renovate update that changes only them merges after green CI (renovate.json,
# automerge). The app is also a bypass actor of the code owner rule for pull
# requests, which lets workflow and development-dependency patch/minor updates
# merge the same way; majors, renovate.json, this file and .releaserc.json do
# not (renovate.json, "Automerge"). The manifests composer.json and package.json stay owned: they
# also carry scripts. renovate.json stays owned too: it decides what merges
# without review. An update that changes a manifest, a workflow, a GitHub
# Action or docker/Dockerfile waits for the maintainer. docker/base-images.env
# holds the base image pins of docker/Dockerfile and nothing else: the
# required check "Base image pins" (scripts/base_images.py) refuses a second
# pin in the Dockerfile and any image that is not on its allowlist, so only a
# tag or digest can change without review.
/composer.lock
/package-lock.json
/.github/release-tools/package-lock.json
/website/package-lock.json
/docker/base-images.env
